Subject: base-files: report an OpenWrt release to third-party scripts

Install scripts of third-party packages read DISTRIB_RELEASE and
VERSION_ID, take the branch out of them and refuse anything that is not
23.05, 24.10 or 25.12. With the version options set for Beam WRT they
saw "1.5.0" and stopped. Keep the identity fields as OpenWrt 25.12.6,
the newest release of the branch this tree is closest to, and leave the
Beam WRT name and version in DISTRIB_DESCRIPTION, PRETTY_NAME and
OPENWRT_RELEASE, where people read it.

--- a/package/base-files/files/etc/openwrt_release
+++ b/package/base-files/files/etc/openwrt_release
@@ -1,5 +1,5 @@
-DISTRIB_ID='%D'
-DISTRIB_RELEASE='%V'
+DISTRIB_ID='OpenWrt'
+DISTRIB_RELEASE='25.12.6'
 DISTRIB_REVISION='%R'
 DISTRIB_TARGET='%S'
 DISTRIB_ARCH='%A'
--- a/package/base-files/files/usr/lib/os-release
+++ b/package/base-files/files/usr/lib/os-release
@@ -1,9 +1,9 @@
-NAME="%D"
-VERSION="%V"
-ID="%d"
+NAME="OpenWrt"
+VERSION="25.12.6"
+ID="openwrt"
 ID_LIKE="lede openwrt"
 PRETTY_NAME="%D %V"
-VERSION_ID="%v"
+VERSION_ID="25.12.6"
 HOME_URL="%u"
 BUG_URL="%b"
 SUPPORT_URL="%s"
